Z||000005||JetroGT||01-16-2000||03:13 AM||||I was just thinking about the lable on the fender. Then I rembered that because it had been hit in the front, the hood is caught on the bolts. You know. The bolts that keep the hood from cutting your head off in a head on collision. I'll just look for over spray and masking lines. From what I could see it looks original. Thanks any way for the cods and that web address!||||reg||11
Z||000006||Phil||01-16-2000||07:15 AM||||Sounds like bent frame time,that could turn out to be a can of worms. Be careful. Did the VIN return a GT? I didn't think there was a non-sunroof version.<p>[This message has been edited by Phil (edited 01-16-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||Wolfhound||01-16-2000||08:07 AM||||Pull off the rear side marker and check for overspray. It would be the rare paintshop that would pull the body panels for painting. May be that the front facia was replaced in a previous accident.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Phil||01-16-2000||10:32 AM||||The shop that's doing my Formula pulled the rockers, front fenders, front and rear facias , lower rear fenders,trunk and hood (I did the molding , mirrors, 1/4 windows and wheel wells) maybe that's why he's had it for 7 weeks so far. "SHOULD" be getting it back this week I hope.||||reg||1
Z||000009||theogre||01-16-2000||11:34 AM||||practically any front end hit can jam the hood. the hinges are fairly weak. you won't know what kind of mess the front is unless you get the hood open. If the hinges are bent enough you might could release teh front hinges from the frame.||||reg||1
Z||000010||JetroGT||01-26-2000||01:11 PM||||It is almost mine!<BR>But now I have to get rid of the other GT. <BR>It's a matter of limited space. You might be thinking, " Why is he getting a another parts GT when he already has one?" This one is almost fully loaded with a 5 Spd. Plus it's a blue 87. Acording to the title it's a one owner car. Now I'm off to the bank!||||reg||10
Z||000011||JetroGT||01-26-2000||07:14 PM||||I drove it to storage today. It drives and shifts great! I didn't get a chance to take a  real close look at the engin but it sounds like an exhaust leak. Probably one of the manifolds. But thats nothing I can't fix. It has that warm burning metal smell. And no, the fiero has not been eating hot peppers.||||reg||6
