Z||000013||JetroGT||01-26-2000||08:02 PM||||I've got tons of V6 parts, too much to list.<P>All of the interior parts are 86/87 GT Gray.<P>I have a drivers side inner door panel for power mirrors with the map pocket. <BR>Extra gauge pod.<BR>One set of plain gray speaker seat covers, Second pair that I found. Very good condition.<BR>Some body panles, but most of them I need.<BR>Carpeting W/ insulation<BR>I know I have some more stuff but the pizzas here. Gotta go.<BR> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000014||JetroGT||02-19-2000||03:21 PM||||A few days ago I found someone who can do frame work. The thing is, this guy didn't get disgusted when I told him that it was a Fiero that I wanted straightened. He acutally went out to the storage place to look at the car. To straighten the frame will run me about $500. I might need a new radiator support. And definatly need a new impact bar. ||||reg||6
Z||000015||Robert||02-19-2000||05:02 PM||||I paid $350 to have my driver’s side frame pulled back out.  It was crushed in about 1 ½”.  They told me it was worth fixing the frame, since the doors still worked properly.    If the doors don’t close, you might be in for BIG bucks.||||reg||1
Z||000016||JetroGT||02-26-2000||02:25 AM||||I made an appoiment to get the GT straightened, repainted, reassembled. I am replacing the hood, both fenders, front cover, impact bar, and the absorber. The guy at the body shop wants to paint the door panles to blend the paint. So I spent the last few days taking my doors apart so that I could take off the mirrors and trim. The GT gets droped off on the first and by the 8th it should be done. Tonight I was busy rebuilding the head light pods. The frame that the motor sits in was broke in half. I had one in my 86 parts car and it worked perfect. After it's fixed I have to decide if I want to sell it or not. The state gave me a new title for it already. They stated that because it was over 7 years old and damaged over 70% of its market value that I did not have to get it inspected. <BR>Woo Hoo!!||||reg||1
